"Outbound Sales": "## What makes it work\n- A tight target list.\n- A message about the prospect's situation, not your product.\n- Patient, polite follow-up.\n- Track replies per target group, so you learn which audience responds.",
"Account-Based Marketing": "## Starting small\n- Pick a short list of accounts.\n- Find two or three people at each.\n- Plan messages that reference the company's own situation.\n- Review each account regularly and drop those that go quiet.",
"CRM": "## Getting value from it\n- Decide which fields are required and stick to them.\n- Log every conversation the same day.\n- Clean duplicates regularly.\n- Choose the simplest system your team will really use every day.",
"Sales Pipeline": "## Keeping it useful\n- Define clear exit criteria for each stage.\n- Review stuck deals every week.\n- Close out deals that will not happen.\n- Record the date each deal entered its stage, so slow deals are easy to see.",
"CRM Data Import": "## Import checklist\n- Back up your CRM first.\n- Map columns and test with a few rows.\n- Remove opted-out contacts before importing.\n- Keep a copy of the original file so you can trace any problem back to its source.",
"Data Segmentation": "## Starting with segments\n- Begin with industry and place, which are easy to get right.\n- Keep each segment large enough to test.\n- Write the message for the segment, not for everyone.",
"Geographic Segmentation": "## Practical tips\n- Use consistent place names.\n- Test in one city first.\n- Mention something local when it is true and useful.\n- Check that place names match across sources, for example abbreviations and spellings.\n- Keep a record of the area each segment covers.\n- Compare results between places before widening a campaign.",
"Industry Segmentation": "## Getting it right\n- Use a clear, consistent category for every record.\n- Learn the vocabulary of the industry.\n- Start with one industry and expand after you see results.",
"Marketing Automation": "## Avoiding common problems\n- Test every rule with a few addresses first.\n- Keep opt-outs working across all automations.\n- Review sent messages regularly for errors.",
"Drip Campaign": "## Planning one\n- Write down the goal of each message.\n- Leave enough time between sends.\n- End the series as soon as the goal is reached.\n- Review each message after a month and rewrite the weakest one.",
